Package: daffiz
Title: Value-by-Value Comparison of Two Tables
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", email = "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Compares two tables value by value. A candidate table can be
    checked against a benchmark whose column types are taken as the truth,
    with the candidate's columns cast to those types first, or two tables can
    be checked for equality as peers. Rows are aligned on their identity
    columns, numeric measures are compared within an optional tolerance, and
    the result is a long 'data.table' with one row per compared value that
    traces back to the source rows of both inputs.
